WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.326
The software development lifecycle is the way an organization plans, designs, builds, tests, releases, operates, and maintains software.

2
00:00:09.326 --> 00:00:18.651
A secure SDLC integrates security into those stages instead of treating security as a final gate after most decisions have already been made.

3
00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:27.271
The point is to make security part of normal engineering work, not a separate inspection that arrives too late to shape the product.

4
00:00:27.271 --> 00:00:32.365
Secure SDLC includes secure coding, but it is broader than coding practices.

5
00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:37.381
Application security testing checks whether controls behave as expected.

6
00:00:37.381 --> 00:00:42.631
DevSecOps emphasizes automation and shared ownership in delivery pipelines.

7
00:00:42.631 --> 00:00:48.822
Software assurance focuses on confidence that software is trustworthy for its intended use.

8
00:00:48.822 --> 00:00:54.386
Governance defines expectations, accountability, evidence, and risk decisions.

9
00:00:54.386 --> 00:00:58.853
These ideas overlap, but none of them alone is the entire lifecycle.

10
00:00:58.853 --> 00:01:04.339
Security defects are usually easier and cheaper to address earlier in the process.

11
00:01:04.339 --> 00:01:15.153
A missing authorization requirement can be corrected quickly during planning, but it may require redesign, data migration, and painful retesting after release.

12
00:01:15.153 --> 00:01:23.930
A risky dependency can be replaced early, while the same issue discovered late may block deployment or force emergency remediation.

13
00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:27.300
Early security work reduces rework and surprises.

14
00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:34.980
A strong secure SDLC supports engineering quality, customer trust, compliance, resilience, and risk management.

15
00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.488
It does not promise perfect software.

16
00:01:37.488 --> 00:01:46.343
It creates repeatable practices that help teams understand risk, make informed tradeoffs, produce evidence, and improve over time.

17
00:01:46.343 --> 00:01:55.042
The goal is software that is safer to build, safer to operate, and easier to maintain under changing business and threat conditions.
